#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cockpit-state — the writer of the cockpit's state file (contract: cockpit/schema.json).

    cockpit-state [--once]              write the file once and exit
    cockpit-state --loop N              write now and every N seconds; leaves when its
                                        parent dies, or (--bind-pane) when the brainer
                                        pane is gone from herdr
    cockpit-state --kick                an EVENT happened: write, debounced to one write
                                        per 250 ms, in the background; returns at once
    cockpit-state --print-path          the state file this brainer's mod reads
    cockpit-state ctx <transcript>      `{"pct":…,"tokens":…}` from the last assistant
                                        usage of a claude transcript (exit 1: none)
    cockpit-state --pilot               the pilot metric: median and p90 time from an envelope
                                        (report, ask, challenge) to the brainer's first action on
                                        its pane, and what has had none for 30 min

    options  --invoker PANE   the brainer whose executors these rows are (default
                              $HW_COCKPIT_INVOKER, else $HERDR_PANE_ID); --rundir DIR
                              names it from that run's env instead. When either flag
                              names a brainer that does not resolve (an empty --invoker,
                              a run env without HW_INVOKER_PANE) nothing falls back to the
                              environment's pane, which in an executor is its own: a kick
                              writes nothing and leaves a line in <work>/.cockpit/skipped-kicks.log
             --state PATH     the file (default $HW_COCKPIT_STATE, else
                              <work>/.cockpit/<invoker>.json)
             --stdout         print instead of writing (nothing is created)

WHAT IT READS: `herdr pane list` (one RPC, ~7 ms with 40 panes), each executor's run
directory (task, markers, hold files, queued rulings, receipt) and the suite gate's
slot directory. NEVER a pane capture per beat — `hw status` reads one per pane, serially, and took 25.5 s
with 31 panes, which is why this exists. The one read it does make is the claude panes' statusline, cached, in
parallel and bounded (see THE CONTEXT OF A CLAUDE CARD). Read-only except its own file: written through
a tmp file and `os.replace` under flock, so a reader sees the old file or the new one,
never half of either, and capped at 256 KiB (rows are dropped from the END, which is the
lowest-ranked, and counted in totals.omitted).

THE ROW'S TRUTH IS ON DISK, NOT IN A TOKEN, wherever a token can outlive its task: an ask
is a valid `pending-reply-<n>` hold in the task's state dir (ask tokens "outlive the task
that opened them", bin/hw `_agent_blocked_on_own_ask`), a report is the task's `done`
marker. A token only fills in what the disk fact does not carry (the summary, the context).

WHAT IT DOES NOT DECIDE: which buttons are valid. That is `bin/hw-actions`, the module
`hw done`, `hw ruling` and `hw receipt` take their refusals from, so a button is false
exactly where the verb would refuse and says the verb's own words.

THE CONTEXT OF A CLAUDE CARD is the pane's own statusline (`Ctx: <tokens> | Ctx Used: <pct>%`), read with
`herdr agent read <pane> --source visible` (the source `hw status` uses): the tokens and the percent of the window
Claude Code really has. It is read at most every 10 s per pane (the cache file below), the panes due side by side,
one bounded wait for all (2 s, up to 32 reads at once). `herdr pane list` stays the only RPC of a beat that has nothing due. The fallbacks
are the turn-end token and the live transcript: they know the tokens and NOT the window, so the percent is null
unless the model id names it (`[1m]`); a card then shows the tokens alone. No window is ever assumed.
(Measured 2026-10-08: a 200k default shown as 100% on a 283.8k-token sonnet-5-5 whose statusline said 28%.)

HOW LONG, AND WHETHER IT MOVES. Every row carries `dispatched_at` (the run's start: the first line of
its receipt, else the dispatch file's mtime, else the env file's) and, for a WORKING row only,
`turn_started_at` and `last_progress_at`. No adapter publishes the start of a turn, so it is derived
from the tokens that exist: the previous turn's `turn_ended_at` (dispatched_at in a first turn), which
overstates a turn that an idle gap preceded. `last_progress_at` is the newest of dispatched_at, the
last commit of the worktree (its HEAD reflog: commit, merge, cherry-pick, revert), the newest file
mtime in the worktree (not .git, .hw, node_modules or other caches) and, for claude, the mtime of the
session transcript. The walk of a worktree costs 65-175 ms per 4.7k files (measured 2026-10-08; a cached answer is a dict lookup, 0.03 ms), so
it runs at most once per 30-60 s per worktree (the TTL is jittered by path so forty worktrees do not
expire on one beat) and its answer lives, with the statuslines', in <state file>.cache, shared by the heartbeat
and the kicks, which are separate processes; `--stdout` reads it and writes nothing. The mark itself
is the mod's: `rules.no_progress_after_ms` (NO_PROGRESS_MS, 30 min) is published so the threshold
exists once.

THE PILOT RECORDER. Every write also appends one line per NEW report, ask or challenge a row
carries (`{"at","pane","task","kind"}`, `at` the envelope's own time) to <state dir>/cockpit-events.jsonl,
deduplicated against the file's tail, rotated to cockpit-events.jsonl.1 at 1 MiB. The mod appends its own
`{"at","pane","verb"}` to cockpit-actions.jsonl beside it (a second file, because the mod's fs can only
rewrite a whole file and would otherwise drop a line this writer appended in between). Both live under
<work>/.cockpit, never in a repo. `--pilot` reads the two.

Environment: HW_COCKPIT_HERDR (the herdr command, default `herdr`; tests stub it),
HW_COCKPIT_WORK / WORK (the work root), HW_BRAIN_ROOT.
"""
import argparse
import datetime
import fcntl
import glob
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import zlib

BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
SCHEMA = 1
CAP_BYTES = 256 * 1024
MAX_ROWS = 64
DEBOUNCE_S = 0.25
ORDER = ["challenge", "ask", "blocked", "report", "working", "idle", "gone"]
SUM_CHUNKS = ["sum"] + ["sum%d" % i for i in range(2, 8)]
TOKEN_WIDTH = 80  # invoker-common.sh INVOKER_TOKEN_CHARS: herdr cuts a token value here
# What `ctx` knows about a model's window: a `[1m]` model id is the 1M window by name; nothing else is assumed.
# Any other window is UNESTABLISHED, so it is not guessed: see ctx_from_transcript.
WINDOW_1M = 1_000_000
# The one threshold of the card's `no progress` mark, published as rules.no_progress_after_ms. The
# environment variable exists for the tests and a probe, never for a person's setup.
NO_PROGRESS_MS = 30 * 60 * 1000
PROGRESS_TTL_S = 30           # a worktree is walked at most this often (plus up to as much again, by path)
PROGRESS_MAX_FILES = 20_000   # a walk gives up here: the newest mtime so far is the answer
PROGRESS_SKIP = {".git", ".hw", "node_modules", ".venv", "venv", "__pycache__", ".next", ".cache", ".pytest_cache", ".mypy_cache", ".gradle"}
CACHE_SUFFIX = ".cache"   # <state file>.cache: one cache per brainer, so two writers never overwrite each other's entries
STATUSLINE_TTL_S = 10         # a pane's statusline is read at most this often
STATUSLINE_TIMEOUT_S = 2      # one bounded wait for all the panes, read side by side (hw status: HW_STATUS_CTX_TIMEOUT)
COMMIT_REFLOG = ("commit", "merge", "cherry-pick", "revert")


def _load(name):
    """A sibling bin/ tool as a module (they have no .py extension)."""
    path = os.path.join(BIN, name)
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name.replace("-", "_"), path)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


# ── small readers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def now_ms():
    return int(time.time() * 1000)


def iso_ms(s):
    """`2026-10-06T14:49:35Z` → epoch ms, None when it is not that."""
    try:
        t = datetime.datetime.strptime(s, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    return int(t.timestamp() * 1000)


def mtime_ms(path):
    try:
        return int(os.path.getmtime(path) * 1000)
    except OSError:
        return None


def read_text(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as fh:
            return fh.read()
    except OSError:
        return None


def to_int(v):
    try:
        return int(str(v).strip())
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def to_float(v):
    try:
        return float(str(v).strip())
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def work_root():
    w = os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_WORK") or os.environ.get("WORK")
    if not w:
        root = os.environ.get("HW_BRAIN_ROOT") or os.path.dirname(BIN)
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(root, "projects.json"), encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                w = json.load(fh).get("work")
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            w = None
    return os.path.expanduser(w) if w else None


def state_path(invoker):
    p = os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_STATE")
    if p:
        return p
    w = work_root()
    if not w or not invoker:
        return None
    return os.path.join(w, ".cockpit", invoker + ".json")


def hw_rev():
    root = os.environ.get("HW_BRAIN_ROOT") or os.path.dirname(BIN)
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD"], capture_output=True,
                           text=True, timeout=2)
        return r.stdout.strip() or "unknown" if r.returncode == 0 else "unknown"
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return "unknown"


# ── herdr ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def herdr_panes():
    """(ok, panes, error). One RPC; any failure is ok=False and rows empty."""
    cmd = os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_HERDR", "herdr")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([cmd, "pane", "list"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return False, [], "herdr pane list failed: %s" % (str(e) or type(e).__name__)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return False, [], "herdr pane list exited %d" % r.returncode
    try:
        panes = json.loads(r.stdout)["result"]["panes"]
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return False, [], "herdr pane list answered something that is not a pane list"
    return True, panes, None


# ── run directories ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def find_rundir(cwd, run):
    """The pane's own run first (bin/state-witness.sh witness_run_dir), up to 12 parents."""
    d = cwd or ""
    for _ in range(12):
        if not d or d == "/":
            break
        cand = os.path.join(d, ".hw", run)
        if run and os.path.isdir(cand):
            return cand
        d = os.path.dirname(d)
    return None


def task_seq(rundir):
    n = to_int("".join(c for c in (read_text(os.path.join(rundir, "task")) or "") if c.isdigit()))
    return n if n and n > 0 else 1


def task_dir(rundir):
    n = task_seq(rundir)
    return rundir if n == 1 else os.path.join(rundir, "t%d" % n)


def receipt_value(rundir, key):
    """The LAST value of `key` in the run's receipt.jsonl, None when absent."""
    val = None
    text = read_text(os.path.join(rundir, "receipt.jsonl")) or ""
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if '"%s"' % key not in line:
            continue
        try:
            o = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if o.get("key") == key:
            val = o.get("value")
    return val


def effort_of(rundir):
    """The run's resolved effort, from the `effort=` line of its dispatch file (the format
    bin/hw's _next_dispatch_effort reads), None when absent or only the agent's own default."""
    for line in (read_text(os.path.join(rundir, "dispatch")) or "").splitlines():
        m = re.match(r"\s*effort=(.*)$", line)
        if m:
            v = re.sub(r"  \([^()]*\)$", "", m.group(1)).strip()
            return None if v in ("", "<agent default>") else v
    return None


def join_chunks(tokens, names):
    """Rejoin a chunked token (`sum`, `sum2` …) into the text it carried.

    herdr TRIMS trailing whitespace from every value (measured on live panes), and
    invoker_chunk_tokens breaks at a space when it can, keeping the space on the chunk
    it ended. So a chunk shorter than the width lost a separator and gets one back; a
    chunk of exactly the width was a hard cut inside a word and gets none.
    """
    out = ""
    present = [tokens[n] for n in names if isinstance(tokens.get(n), str) and tokens[n] != ""]
    for i, c in enumerate(present):
        out += c
        if i < len(present) - 1 and len(c) < TOKEN_WIDTH:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M07
            out += " "
    return out


# ── the context a pane's statusline says ─────────────────────────────────────

def statusline_parse(text):
    """(tokens, percent|None) from the last statusline row of a pane screen (`Model: … | Ctx: <n> | Ctx Used:
    <p>% | …`), or None when there is none. Claude Code's own account of its context, and what `hw status` reads
    (lib/hw/status.sh pane_ctx_parse, kept in step by hand). The row is found by `Ctx:`, not by `Ctx Used:`: a
    narrow pane cuts the footer to `Ctx: 237.5k | Ctx Use…`, so the percent is optional."""
    rows = [l for l in (text or "").replace("\u00a0", " ").splitlines() if re.search(r"Ctx: *[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?[kKmM]? *\|", l)]
    if not rows:
        return None
    m = re.search(r"Ctx: *([0-9.]+)([kKmM]?)", rows[-1])
    u = re.search(r"Ctx Used: *([0-9.]+)", rows[-1])
    if not m:
        return None
    mult = {"k": 1000, "m": 1000000}.get(m.group(2).lower(), 1)
    try:
        return int(float(m.group(1)) * mult), (float(u.group(1)) if u else None)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M04
    except ValueError:  # `Ctx: 1.2.3`: not a measurement
        return None


def statusline_read(pane_id, timeout):
    """One bounded `herdr agent read <pane> --source visible`: the parsed statusline, None when the pane has none,
    cannot be read or does not answer in time. The child gets its own process group so a hang is killed whole."""
    cmd = os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_HERDR", "herdr")
    try:
        p = subprocess.Popen([cmd, "agent", "read", pane_id, "--source", "visible"], stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                             stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True, errors="replace", start_new_session=True)
    except OSError:
        return None
    try:
        out, _ = p.communicate(timeout=timeout)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M05
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        try:
            os.killpg(p.pid, 9)
        except OSError:
            pass
        try:
            p.communicate(timeout=1)
        except subprocess.SubprocessError:
            pass
        return None
    return statusline_parse(out) if p.returncode == 0 else None


def statuslines(pane_ids, now):
    """{pane: (tokens, pct|None) | None}. Each pane is read once per STATUSLINE_TTL_S (shared by the writers through
    the cache file, a miss included), the ones due side by side so the whole beat costs one timeout at worst."""
    ttl = env_seconds("HW_COCKPIT_CTX_TTL_S", STATUSLINE_TTL_S) * 1000
    timeout = env_seconds("HW_COCKPIT_CTX_TIMEOUT_S", STATUSLINE_TIMEOUT_S)
    out, due = {}, []
    for pid in sorted({p for p in pane_ids if p}):
        key = "pane:" + pid
        _CACHE_SEEN.add(key)
        hit = _CACHE.get(key)
        if hit and 0 <= now - hit[0] < ttl:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M03
            out[pid] = None if hit[1] is None else (int(hit[1]), hit[2])
        else:
            due.append(pid)
    if due:
        from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor
        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=min(32, len(due))) as ex:  # one timeout for the lot, not one per batch of 8
            for pid, got in zip(due, ex.map(lambda x: statusline_read(x, timeout), due)):
                out[pid] = got
                _CACHE["pane:" + pid] = [now, None, None] if got is None else [now, got[0], got[1]]
    return out


# ── how long it has worked, and whether it moves ─────────────────────────────

def env_seconds(name, default_s):
    v = to_int(os.environ.get(name))
    return default_s if v is None or v < 0 else v


def no_progress_ms():
    return env_seconds("HW_COCKPIT_NO_PROGRESS_S", NO_PROGRESS_MS // 1000) * 1000  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M02


def dispatched_at_of(rundir):
    """When the run began: the `at` of the first receipt line that has one, else the dispatch file's
    mtime, else the env file's (hw writes all three at dispatch)."""
    for line in (read_text(os.path.join(rundir, "receipt.jsonl")) or "").splitlines():
        try:
            at = iso_ms(json.loads(line).get("at"))
        except (ValueError, AttributeError):
            continue
        if at is not None:
            return at
    for name in ("dispatch", "env"):
        m = mtime_ms(os.path.join(rundir, name))
        if m is not None:
            return m
    return now_ms()


def gitdir_of(root):
    """The git directory of a worktree: `.git` itself, or what a linked worktree's `.git` file points to."""
    g = os.path.join(root, ".git")
    if os.path.isdir(g):
        return g
    m = re.match(r"gitdir:\s*(.+)", read_text(g) or "")
    if not m:
        return None
    d = m.group(1).strip()
    return d if os.path.isabs(d) else os.path.normpath(os.path.join(root, d))


def last_commit_ms(root):
    """The time of the worktree's last commit (and merge, cherry-pick, revert), from the tail of its HEAD
    reflog: no subprocess, no base to name. A checkout, a branch creation or a rebase's bookkeeping are not work."""
    gd = gitdir_of(root)
    if not gd:
        return None
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(gd, "logs", "HEAD"), "rb") as fh:
            fh.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            fh.seek(max(0, fh.tell() - 16384))
            tail = fh.read().decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return None
    for line in reversed(tail.splitlines()):
        m = re.search(r"> (\d+) [+-]\d{4}\t(\S+)", line)
        if m and m.group(2).rstrip(":") in COMMIT_REFLOG:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M01
            return int(m.group(1)) * 1000
    return None


def progress_ttl_ms(root):
    base = env_seconds("HW_COCKPIT_PROGRESS_TTL_S", PROGRESS_TTL_S)
    return 0 if base == 0 else (base + zlib.crc32(root.encode()) % base) * 1000


def newest_mtime_ms(root, cache, now):
    """The newest file mtime under `root` (not PROGRESS_SKIP, no symlinks), None when there is no file.
    `cache` maps root -> [walked_at_ms, newest]: a root walked less than its TTL ago is not walked again."""
    hit = cache.get(root)
    if hit and 0 <= now - hit[0] < progress_ttl_ms(root):  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M03
        return hit[1]
    newest, seen, stack = None, 0, [root]
    while stack and seen < PROGRESS_MAX_FILES:
        try:
            it = os.scandir(stack.pop())
        except OSError:
            continue
        with it:
            for e in it:
                try:
                    if e.is_symlink():
                        continue
                    if e.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False):
                        if e.name not in PROGRESS_SKIP:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M04
                            stack.append(e.path)
                        continue
                    m = int(e.stat(follow_symlinks=False).st_mtime * 1000)
                except OSError:
                    continue
                seen += 1
                if newest is None or m > newest:
                    newest = m
    cache[root] = [now, newest]
    return newest


_CACHE = {}       # worktree root -> [walked_at_ms, newest mtime or None], "pane:<id>" -> [read_at_ms, tokens, pct]; shared through the cache file
_CACHE_SEEN = set()


def cache_entry_ok(k, v):
    num = lambda x: x is None or (isinstance(x, (int, float)) and not isinstance(x, bool))
    if not isinstance(v, list) or not v or not isinstance(v[0], int):
        return False
    return (len(v) == 3 and all(num(x) for x in v[1:])) if k.startswith("pane:") else (len(v) == 2 and num(v[1]))


def load_cache(path):
    """Merge the cache file beside the state file into this process's: the newer walk of each root wins."""
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            data = json.load(fh)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return
    for k, v in (data.items() if isinstance(data, dict) else ()):
        if cache_entry_ok(k, v):
            if k not in _CACHE or v[0] > _CACHE[k][0]:
                _CACHE[k] = v


def save_cache(path):
    """Write the entries this build used (the rest is dead weight), through a tmp file; never raises."""
    try:
        keep = {k: v for k, v in _CACHE.items() if k in _CACHE_SEEN}
        tmp = "%s.tmp.%d" % (path, os.getpid())
        with os.fdopen(os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            json.dump(keep, fh)
        os.replace(tmp, path)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M07
    except OSError as e:
        print("cockpit-state: could not save the cache: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)


def transcript_mtime_ms(rundir, env):
    path = transcript_of(rundir, env)
    return mtime_ms(path) if path else None


def last_progress_of(rundir, env, harness, dispatched):
    """The newest sign that the executor is working, never later than now. dispatched_at is the floor."""
    root = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(rundir.rstrip("/")))  # <cwd>/.hw/<run>
    now = now_ms()
    _CACHE_SEEN.add(root)
    signs = [dispatched, last_commit_ms(root), newest_mtime_ms(root, _CACHE, now)]
    if harness == "claude":  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M06
        try:
            signs.append(transcript_mtime_ms(rundir, env))
        except Exception:
            pass  # a transcript nobody foresaw is no sign, not a failed row
    return min(now, max(x for x in signs if x is not None))


# ── the row ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def pending_rulings(rundir):
    ages = []
    for f in glob.glob(os.path.join(rundir, "pending-ruling*")):
        n = os.path.basename(f)[len("pending-ruling"):]
        if (n == "" or re.fullmatch(r"\.\d+", n)) and os.path.isfile(f):
            m = mtime_ms(f)
            if m is not None:
                ages.append(m)
    return {"count": min(len(ages), 5), "oldest_at": min(ages) if ages else None}


def ask_of(rundir, tdir, pane_id, run, vendor, tokens, hold):
    """The outstanding ask or challenge, from its hold file; None when nothing is owed.

    `pending_reply` is the hold's path only when the reply verbs would be accepted:
    the hold is valid for THIS pane (holdfacts, the validator channel-send itself asks)
    and its route is herdr, which is what the verbs name.
    """
    best = None
    for f in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(tdir, "pending-reply-*"))):
        facts, err = hold.read_facts(f)
        if facts is None:
            continue
        m = re.fullmatch(re.escape(run) + r"(?::t\d+)?:(ask|challenge):([1-9][0-9]*):reply", facts.get("logical_id", ""))
        if not m:
            continue
        kind, n = m.group(1), int(m.group(2))
        at = mtime_ms(f) or 0
        valid = hold.problem(facts, run, pane_id, vendor) is None and facts.get("route") == "herdr"  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M08
        label = tokens.get("ask_seq") if re.fullmatch(r"%d/\d+" % n, tokens.get("ask_seq") or "") else "%d/3" % n
        cand = {"kind": kind, "seq": label,
                "state": "delivered" if facts.get("state") == "delivered" else "undelivered",
                "at": at, "pending_reply": os.path.abspath(f) if valid else None}
        if best is None or at >= best["at"]:
            best = cand
    return best


def report_of(rundir, tdir, tokens, blocked_waiting):
    """The current task's report, or None. The `done` marker is the fact; done tokens
    outlive a task like ask tokens do, so they only count with it, or when they say the
    report was never delivered (then there is no marker to find)."""
    marker = os.path.join(tdir, "done")
    has_marker = os.path.isfile(marker) and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(tdir, "reopened"))  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M09
    status = tokens.get("done_status")
    done_at = iso_ms(tokens.get("done_at"))
    stranded = False
    if not has_marker:
        if status in ("done", "blocked") and tokens.get("done_state") == "undelivered" and done_at is not None:
            floor = mtime_ms(os.path.join(rundir, "task")) if tdir != rundir else 0
            stranded = done_at >= (floor or 0)
        if not stranded:
            return None
    if status not in ("done", "blocked"):
        status = "blocked" if blocked_waiting else (receipt_value(rundir, "report_status") or "done")
        if status not in ("done", "blocked"):
            status = "done"
    summary = join_chunks(tokens, SUM_CHUNKS) if tokens.get("done_status") else ""
    if not summary:
        summary = str(receipt_value(rundir, "report_summary") or "")
    artifacts = to_int(tokens.get("artifacts")) if tokens.get("done_status") else None
    if artifacts is None:
        artifacts = to_int(receipt_value(rundir, "report_artifacts")) or 0
    engram = tokens.get("engram") if tokens.get("done_status") else None
    if not engram:
        engram = receipt_value(rundir, "report_engram") or None
    seq = task_seq(rundir)
    prefix = os.path.basename(rundir) + ("" if seq == 1 else ":t%d" % seq)
    return {"envelope_id": prefix + ":done", "status": status,
            "state": "undelivered" if (tokens.get("done_state") == "undelivered" and done_at is not None) else "delivered",
            "at": done_at if done_at is not None else (mtime_ms(marker) or 0),
            "summary": summary[:640], "artifacts": artifacts, "engram": engram if isinstance(engram, str) else None}


def ctx_of(tokens):
    pct, toks = to_float(tokens.get("ctx_pct")), to_int(tokens.get("ctx_tokens"))
    if toks is None or toks < 0:
        return {"pct": None, "tokens": None, "source": None}
    # `ctx_pct` is "null" when the hook's transcript names no window: the tokens stand, the percent is unknown
    return {"pct": pct if pct is not None and 0 <= pct <= 100 else None, "tokens": toks, "source": "turn-end"}


# THE LIVE READ. A turn-end token only exists once a turn has ended, and an executor in its first
# long turn (hours) has none, so its card said `ctx n/a` for exactly the time the number matters.
# The transcript is on disk the whole time: resolved from facts the run already has, read with
# ctx_from_transcript (the tail only) and cached by (mtime, size), so a beat over a transcript that
# did not move costs one stat. The loop is one process, so the cache lives across beats.
_LIVE = {}         # transcript path -> ((mtime_ns, size), ctx or None)
_TRANSCRIPTS = {}  # (config dir, session id) -> transcript path
CACHE_MAX = 256


def transcript_of(rundir, env):
    """The claude transcript of the run's session, None when it does not resolve.

    Session id: the receipt's `session_id` (hw writes it after the brief lands). Directory:
    `$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` from the run env (the account travels there, default ~/.claude) +
    `projects/<launch cwd, non-alphanumerics as "-">/<session>.jsonl`; when that name does not
    exist, the session id is a uuid and the one match under projects/ is it."""
    sid = receipt_value(rundir, "session_id")
    if not isinstance(sid, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9A-Za-z-]{8,64}", sid):
        return None
    cfg = os.path.expanduser(env.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or "~/.claude")
    key = (cfg, sid)
    hit = _TRANSCRIPTS.get(key)
    if hit and os.path.isfile(hit):
        return hit
    launch = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(rundir.rstrip("/")))  # <cwd>/.hw/<run>
    found = None
    for cwd in dict.fromkeys((launch, os.path.realpath(launch))):
        cand = os.path.join(cfg, "projects", re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9]", "-", cwd), sid + ".jsonl")
        if os.path.isfile(cand):
            found = cand
            break
    if not found:
        found = next(iter(sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(cfg), "projects", "*", sid + ".jsonl")))), None)
    if found:
        _TRANSCRIPTS[key] = found
    return found


def live_ctx(rundir, env):
    """(ctx, transcript mtime in ms) of the run's session, (None, None) when it does not resolve or
    holds no usage yet."""
    path = transcript_of(rundir, env)
    if not path:
        return None, None
    try:
        st = os.stat(path)
    except OSError:
        return None, None
    sig = (st.st_mtime_ns, st.st_size)
    hit = _LIVE.get(path)
    if hit is None or hit[0] != sig:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M26
        if len(_LIVE) >= CACHE_MAX:
            _LIVE.clear()
        hit = _LIVE[path] = (sig, ctx_from_transcript(path))
    return hit[1], int(st.st_mtime_ns // 1_000_000)


def executor_run(pane, invoker, mods):
    """(rundir, env) of the run this pane is an executor of for `invoker`, None when it is not one of its executors."""
    tokens = pane.get("tokens") or {}
    task, run = tokens.get("hw_task"), tokens.get("hw_run")
    if not task or not run:
        return None
    rundir = find_rundir(pane.get("cwd"), run)
    if not rundir:
        return None
    env = mods["runenv"].read(rundir, lenient=True) or {}
    if env.get("HW_INVOKER_PANE") != invoker:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M03
        return None
    return rundir, env


def is_claude_executor(pane, invoker, mods):
    found = executor_run(pane, invoker, mods)
    return bool(found) and found[1].get("HW_EXECUTOR_VENDOR") == "claude"


def build_row(pane, invoker, mods, sl=None):
    """One row, or None when this pane is not an executor of `invoker`."""
    found = executor_run(pane, invoker, mods)
    if not found:
        return None
    rundir, env = found
    tokens = pane.get("tokens") or {}
    task, run = tokens.get("hw_task"), tokens.get("hw_run")
    project = tokens.get("hw_project") or env.get("HW_PROJECT") or "unknown"
    tdir = task_dir(rundir)
    harness = env.get("HW_EXECUTOR_VENDOR")
    vendor = harness if harness in ("claude", "opencode", "codex") else "unknown"
    pane_id = pane.get("pane_id")
    blocked_waiting = os.path.isfile(os.path.join(tdir, "blocked-waiting"))
    report = report_of(rundir, tdir, tokens, blocked_waiting)
    ask = None if report else ask_of(rundir, tdir, pane_id, run, vendor, tokens, mods["holdfacts"])
    status = pane.get("agent_status")
    status = status if status in ("idle", "working", "unknown") else "unknown"
    turn_state = tokens.get("turn_state")
    if turn_state not in ("working", "ended_unreported", "ended_after_report", "ended_with_ruling", "ended_holding",
                          "ended_human_boundary", "ended_awaiting_child", "handback_refused"):
        turn_state = None
    turn_at = iso_ms(tokens.get("turn_ended_at"))
    children = tokens.get("children_running") or None

    if ask:
        attention, since = ask["kind"], ask["at"]
    elif report:
        attention = "blocked" if report["status"] == "blocked" else "report"
        since = report["at"]
    elif status == "working" or (turn_state == "ended_awaiting_child" and children):
        attention, since = "working", turn_at
    else:
        attention, since = "idle", turn_at

    ctx = ctx_of(tokens)
    if attention == "working" and harness == "claude":  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M25
        # The turn-end value stands when it is newer than the transcript; otherwise (no value
        # yet, or the transcript moved since) the live one does.
        try:
            live, live_at = live_ctx(rundir, env)
        except Exception:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M28  # a transcript line of a shape nobody foresaw must not take the file down: the card keeps its turn-end value, or n/a
            live, live_at = None, None
        if live and (ctx["tokens"] is None or turn_at is None or live_at > turn_at):  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M27
            ctx = {"pct": live["pct"], "tokens": live["tokens"], "source": "live"}
    # THE SOURCE OF TRUTH is the pane's own statusline, which carries Claude Code's tokens and its percent of the
    # window it really has. Everything above is the fallback: a transcript knows the tokens, never the window.
    shown = (sl or {}).get(pane_id) if harness == "claude" else None
    if shown:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M01
        ctx = {"pct": shown[1], "tokens": shown[0], "source": "statusline"}

    dispatched = dispatched_at_of(rundir)
    turn_started = progress = None
    if attention == "working":
        turn_started = max(turn_at, dispatched) if turn_at is not None else dispatched  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M05
        progress = last_progress_of(rundir, env, harness, dispatched)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 920-M08

    try:
        facts = mods["actions"].facts_from_pane(pane, rundir)
        actions = mods["actions"].actions_for_row(facts)
    except Exception as e:  # one row must not take the file down; say so where the button is
        why = "cockpit-state could not evaluate this row: %s" % (str(e) or type(e).__name__)
        actions = {"verify": False, "ruling": False, "done": False, "receipt": False,
                   "why_not": {"verify": why, "ruling": why, "done": why, "receipt": why}}

    return {
        "id": "%s:%s" % (project, task), "project": project, "task": task, "pane": pane_id, "run": run,
        "task_n": task_seq(rundir), "vendor": harness or "unknown", "model": receipt_value(rundir, "model_running") or None,
        "effort": effort_of(rundir),
        "agent_status": status, "turn_state": turn_state, "turn_ended_at": turn_at,
        "dispatched_at": dispatched, "turn_started_at": turn_started, "last_progress_at": progress,
        "turns": to_int(tokens.get("turns")), "children_running": children, "ctx": ctx,
        "rulings_pending": pending_rulings(rundir), "attention": attention, "attention_since": since,
        "report": report, "ask": ask, "actions": actions,
    }


def cut_state(work):
    """Is a release cut holding a suite-gate slot? Its slot's `owner.cmd` starts
    `release cut` (setup/release/cut: sg_take "release cut $VERSION" cut)."""
    off = {"running": False, "since_ms": None, "holder": None}
    if not work:
        return off
    for slot in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(work, ".locks", "suite-gate", "slot.*"))):
        cmd = (read_text(os.path.join(slot, "owner.cmd")) or "").strip()
        pid = to_int(read_text(os.path.join(slot, "owner.pid")))
        if not cmd.startswith("release cut") or not pid:
            continue
        try:
            os.kill(pid, 0)
        except OSError:
            continue
        try:
            start = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "lstart=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True,
                                   timeout=2).stdout
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            continue
        if " ".join(start.split()) != " ".join((read_text(os.path.join(slot, "owner.start")) or "").split()):  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M16
            continue
        at = to_int(read_text(os.path.join(slot, "owner.at")))
        task = (read_text(os.path.join(slot, "owner.task")) or "").strip()
        return {"running": True, "since_ms": at * 1000 if at else None, "holder": task or cmd}
    return off


def key_of(r):
    return (ORDER.index(r["attention"]), r["attention_since"] or 0, r["id"])  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M10


def totals_of(rows, omitted):
    def n(a):
        return sum(1 for r in rows if r["attention"] == a)
    return {"executors": len(rows), "omitted": omitted, "working": n("working"), "idle": n("idle"),
            "asks": n("ask"), "reports": n("report"), "blocked": n("blocked"), "challenges": n("challenge"),
            "rulings_pending": sum(r["rulings_pending"]["count"] for r in rows)}


def build_state(invoker, seq, interval_s, rev, now=None):
    mods = {"runenv": _load("runenv"), "holdfacts": _load("holdfacts"), "actions": _load("hw-actions")}
    ok, panes, err = herdr_panes()
    rows = []
    if ok:
        seen = {}
        now = now_ms()
        # only this brainer's claude executors: another lane's panes are not read (and not cached) by this writer
        claude_panes = [p for p in panes if p.get("agent") == "claude"]
        sl = statuslines([p.get("pane_id") for p in claude_panes if is_claude_executor(p, invoker, mods)], now)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M06
        for p in panes:
            r = build_row(p, invoker, mods, sl)
            if r is None:
                continue
            # one task, one row: a re-dispatch leaves its old pane around, the newest run wins
            if r["id"] in seen and seen[r["id"]]["run"] >= r["run"]:
                continue
            seen[r["id"]] = r
        rows = sorted(seen.values(), key=key_of)
    omitted = max(0, len(rows) - MAX_ROWS)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M12
    rows = rows[:MAX_ROWS]
    state = {"schema": SCHEMA, "generated_at": now if now is not None else now_ms(),
             "writer": {"pid": os.getpid(), "hw_rev": rev, "seq": seq, "interval_s": interval_s},
             "invoker_pane": invoker,
             "herdr": {"ok": ok, "server_started_ms": None, "error": err},
             "totals": totals_of(rows, omitted), "rules": {"cut": cut_state(work_root()), "no_progress_after_ms": no_progress_ms()}, "rows": rows}
    return fit(state)


_ESC_SEQ = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-9;?]*[ -/]*[@-~]|\x1b[@-_]")
_CTRL = re.compile(r"[\x00-\x1f\x7f-\x9f]")


def clean_text(v):
    """One published string with no control character: an escape sequence or a control byte
    becomes a space, runs of spaces collapse. The pane refuses a text child holding one."""
    return re.sub(" +", " ", _CTRL.sub(" ", _ESC_SEQ.sub(" ", v))).strip()


def clean(v):
    if isinstance(v, str):
        return clean_text(v)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M24
    if isinstance(v, list):
        return [clean(x) for x in v]
    if isinstance(v, dict):
        return {k: clean(x) for k, x in v.items()}
    return v


def serialize(state):
    """The one place a state becomes bytes, so the one place every string is cleaned."""
    return json.dumps(clean(state), indent=1) + "\n"


def fit(state):
    """Cap the file as WRITTEN (indented) at 256 KiB by dropping rows from the end (lowest rank)."""
    while len(serialize(state).encode()) > CAP_BYTES and state["rows"]:
        state["rows"].pop()  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M04
        state["totals"] = totals_of(state["rows"], state["totals"]["omitted"] + 1)
    return state


# ── the pilot recorder ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

EVENTS = "cockpit-events.jsonl"
ACTIONS = "cockpit-actions.jsonl"
EVENTS_CAP = 1024 * 1024
TAIL_BYTES = 256 * 1024
MISSED_MS = 30 * 60 * 1000


def read_jsonl(path, tail=None):
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            if tail:
                fh.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
                fh.seek(max(0, fh.tell() - tail))
            data = fh.read().decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return []
    out = []
    for line in data.split("\n"):
        try:
            v = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if isinstance(v, dict):
            out.append(v)
    return out


def events_of(state):
    for r in state["rows"]:
        if r.get("report"):
            yield {"at": r["report"]["at"], "pane": r["pane"], "task": r["task"], "kind": "report"}
        if r.get("ask"):
            yield {"at": r["ask"]["at"], "pane": r["pane"], "task": r["task"], "kind": r["ask"]["kind"]}


def record_events(state, path):
    """Append the events not already in the file's tail. Never raises: the recorder must not take
    the state file down with it."""
    try:
        new = [e for e in events_of(state) if isinstance(e["at"], int)]
        if not new:
            return
        f = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(path), EVENTS)
        with open(f + ".lock", "a") as lock:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            seen = {(e.get("at"), e.get("pane"), e.get("task"), e.get("kind")) for e in read_jsonl(f, TAIL_BYTES)}
            lines = [json.dumps(e, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n" for e in new
                     if (e["at"], e["pane"], e["task"], e["kind"]) not in seen]
            if not lines:
                return
            try:
                if os.path.getsize(f) >= EVENTS_CAP:
                    os.replace(f, f + ".1")
            except OSError:
                pass
            fd = os.open(f, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_APPEND, 0o600)
            try:
                os.write(fd, "".join(lines).encode())
            finally:
                os.close(fd)
    except Exception as e:
        print("cockpit-state: could not record events: %s" % (str(e) or type(e).__name__), file=sys.stderr)


def pilot(cdir, now):
    ev = read_jsonl(os.path.join(cdir, EVENTS + ".1")) + read_jsonl(os.path.join(cdir, EVENTS))
    ac = read_jsonl(os.path.join(cdir, ACTIONS + ".1")) + read_jsonl(os.path.join(cdir, ACTIONS))
    acts = {}
    for a in ac:
        if isinstance(a.get("at"), int) and a.get("pane"):
            acts.setdefault(a["pane"], []).append(a["at"])
    times, missed = [], []
    for e in ev:
        if not isinstance(e.get("at"), int):
            continue
        later = [t for t in acts.get(e.get("pane"), []) if t >= e["at"]]
        if later:
            times.append(min(later) - e["at"])
        elif now - e["at"] > MISSED_MS:
            missed.append(e)
    times.sort()

    def q(p):  # nearest rank
        return times[max(0, -(-p * len(times) // 100) - 1)]
    return times, q, missed


def run_pilot(cdir):
    now = to_int(os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_NOW_MS")) or now_ms()
    times, q, missed = pilot(cdir, now)
    if times:
        print("acted on %d envelopes: median %.1fs, p90 %.1fs" % (len(times), q(50) / 1000, q(90) / 1000))
    else:
        print("acted on 0 envelopes: median -, p90 -")
    print("no action after 30 min: %d" % len(missed))
    for e in missed:
        print("  %s %s %s (%d min ago)" % (e["pane"], e["task"], e["kind"], (now - e["at"]) // 60000))
    return 0


# ── writing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def write_once(invoker, path, interval_s, rev, to_stdout=False):
    if to_stdout:
        if path:  # read what the writers cached; --stdout creates nothing
            load_cache(path + CACHE_SUFFIX)
        print(serialize(build_state(invoker, 0, interval_s, rev)), end="")
        return 0
    if not path:
        print("cockpit-state: no state path (no work root, and no HW_COCKPIT_STATE)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    lock = open(path + ".lock", "a")
    deadline = time.time() + 3
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            break
        except OSError:
            if time.time() > deadline:
                return 0  # another writer is mid-write; its file is as new as ours
            time.sleep(0.02)
    try:
        prev = 0
        try:
            with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                prev = int(json.load(fh)["writer"]["seq"])
        except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
            prev = 0
        cache_file = path + CACHE_SUFFIX  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M07
        load_cache(cache_file)
        _CACHE_SEEN.clear()
        body = serialize(build_state(invoker, prev + 1, interval_s, rev))
        save_cache(cache_file)
        tmp = "%s.tmp.%d" % (path, os.getpid())
        # 0600: the rows carry report summaries, which are the brainer's to read and nobody else's
        with os.fdopen(os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M20
            fh.write(body)
        os.replace(tmp, path)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M01
        record_events(json.loads(body), path)
        clean_stale_tmps(path)
    finally:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        lock.close()
    return 0


def clean_stale_tmps(path):
    """A writer killed between creating its tmp file and the rename leaves the tmp behind (the
    state file itself is untouched: that is the point of the rename). Called under the flock, so
    no live writer is mid-write: any tmp whose pid is gone is garbage."""
    for t in glob.glob(path + ".tmp.*"):
        pid = to_int(t.rsplit(".", 1)[1])
        if not pid or pid == os.getpid():
            continue
        try:
            os.kill(pid, 0)
        except OSError:
            os.unlink(t)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M22


def kick(invoker, path):
    """An event. The claim is a directory: whoever makes it owns the next write, which
    happens DEBOUNCE_S later and reads the state as it is THEN, so every event that
    arrives in between is covered by that one write (trailing-edge coalescing)."""
    if not path:
        return 0
    claim = path + ".kick"
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    try:
        os.mkdir(claim)
    except FileExistsError:
        age = time.time() - (os.path.getmtime(claim) if os.path.exists(claim) else 0)
        if age < 5:
            return 0  # a pending write will include this event  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M02
        try:
            os.rmdir(claim)
            os.mkdir(claim)
        except OSError:
            return 0
    except OSError:
        return 0
    subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, os.path.realpath(__file__), "--kick-run", "--invoker", invoker, "--state", path],
                     stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                     start_new_session=True)
    return 0


def kick_run(invoker, path):
    time.sleep(DEBOUNCE_S)
    try:
        os.rmdir(path + ".kick")  # release BEFORE reading, so an event during the write re-arms
    except OSError:
        pass
    return write_once(invoker, path, 5, hw_rev())


def loop(invoker, path, every, bind_pane):
    """The heartbeat. Two lifetimes, never both:

    · default — it dies with the shell that started it (parent pid changes, or was already
      1 when it booted: python takes ~100 ms to start and the shell may be gone by then);
    · --bind-pane — it is detached (`bin/brain` starts it and exits, claude runs in the PANE,
      not under brain) and dies with the brainer's pane: gone from `herdr pane list`, the
      next beat leaves. A herdr that does not answer keeps it alive writing herdr.ok:false —
      an outage is not a closed pane. ONE per brainer: a second one finds the lock held and
      leaves, so a repeated `brain` start never stacks writers.
    """
    lock = None
    if bind_pane and path:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        lock = open(path + ".loop.lock", "a")
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M19
        except OSError:
            return 0
    ppid, rev = os.getppid(), hw_rev()
    if not bind_pane and ppid == 1:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M17
        return 0  # orphaned before it started (the shell that launched it already exited)
    while True:
        if bind_pane:
            ok, panes, _ = herdr_panes()
            if ok and not any(p.get("pane_id") == invoker for p in panes):  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M18
                return 0  # the brainer's pane is gone: this writer dies with it
        try:
            write_once(invoker, path, every, rev)
        except Exception as e:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M21  # one bad beat (a full disk, a herdr hiccup in a reader) must not end the heartbeat
            print("cockpit-state: write failed: %s" % (str(e) or type(e).__name__), file=sys.stderr)
        if not bind_pane and os.getppid() != ppid:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M11
            return 0  # the brainer's shell is gone: this writer dies with the pane
        time.sleep(every)


# ── ctx ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def ctx_from_transcript(path):
    """{"pct","tokens"} from the last main-thread assistant usage, or None.

    tokens = input + cache_read + cache_creation, the number the statusline shows
    (MEASURED, probe P5). The window is NOT assumed: a model id that says `[1m]` names a 1M window; any other
    id names none, so the percent is null and the tokens stand alone. (It used to read every other model as
    200k and showed 100% on a 283.8k-token sonnet-5-5 whose statusline said 28%, 2026-10-08.)"""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            fh.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            size = fh.tell()
            fh.seek(max(0, size - 512 * 1024))
            tail = fh.read().decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines()
    except OSError:
        return None
    for line in reversed(tail):
        if '"usage"' not in line:
            continue
        try:
            o = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        msg = o.get("message") or {}
        u = msg.get("usage")
        if o.get("type") != "assistant" or o.get("isSidechain") or not isinstance(u, dict):
            continue
        toks = sum(int(u.get(k) or 0) for k in ("input_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens", "cache_creation_input_tokens"))
        if toks <= 0:
            continue
        window = WINDOW_1M if "[1m]" in str(msg.get("model", "")) else None  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M15  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 922-M02
        return {"pct": None if window is None else round(min(100.0, toks * 100.0 / window), 1), "tokens": toks}
    return None


# ── main ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def invoker_of_rundir(rundir):
    """The brainer a run reports to. A chained task keeps its state in `<run>/t<N>` and the env
    file stays in the run directory itself."""
    rundir = rundir.rstrip("/")
    if re.fullmatch(r"t\d+", os.path.basename(rundir)):
        rundir = os.path.dirname(rundir)
    return (_load("runenv").read(rundir, lenient=True) or {}).get("HW_INVOKER_PANE")


def note_skipped_kick(a):
    """A kick that named a brainer it could not resolve: one line in <work>/.cockpit/skipped-kicks.log
    (the callers discard stderr, so a file is the only place it can be read). Best effort, bounded."""
    w = work_root()
    line = "%s kick skipped: no brainer pane from %s\n" % (
        time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"), ("--rundir " + a.rundir) if a.rundir else "an empty --invoker")
    sys.stderr.write("cockpit-state: " + line)
    if not w:
        return
    try:
        d = os.path.join(w, ".cockpit")
        os.makedirs(d, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        f = os.path.join(d, "skipped-kicks.log")
        if os.path.exists(f) and os.path.getsize(f) > 65536:
            return
        with open(f, "a") as fh:
            fh.write(line)
    except OSError:
        pass


def main(argv):
    if len(argv) >= 2 and argv[0] == "ctx":
        c = ctx_from_transcript(argv[1])
        if c is None:
            return 1
        print(json.dumps(c))
        return 0
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="cockpit-state", add_help=True)
    ap.add_argument("--once", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--loop", type=int, metavar="N")
    ap.add_argument("--kick", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--kick-run", action="store_true", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    ap.add_argument("--print-path", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--bind-pane", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--pilot", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--stdout", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--invoker")
    ap.add_argument("--rundir")
    ap.add_argument("--state")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if a.pilot:
        w = work_root()
        cdir = os.path.dirname(a.state or os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_STATE") or "") or (w and os.path.join(w, ".cockpit"))
        if not cdir:
            print("cockpit-state: no state dir (no work root, and no HW_COCKPIT_STATE)", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        return run_pilot(cdir)
    invoker = a.invoker or (invoker_of_rundir(a.rundir) if a.rundir else None)
    if not invoker and (a.invoker is not None or a.rundir):  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 797-M23
        # The caller NAMED a brainer (an executor's kick, from the invoker it was dispatched by)
        # and it did not resolve. The environment's pane is then the executor's own: writing
        # to it would draw a cockpit for a pane that is no brainer. Kick nothing, say so.
        note_skipped_kick(a)
        return 0 if (a.kick or a.kick_run) else 2
    invoker = invoker or os.environ.get("HW_COCKPIT_INVOKER") or os.environ.get("HERDR_PANE_ID")
    if not invoker:
        print("cockpit-state: no brainer pane (--invoker, $HW_COCKPIT_INVOKER or $HERDR_PANE_ID)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    path = a.state or state_path(invoker)
    if a.print_path:
        if not path:
            return 2
        print(path)
        return 0
    if a.kick:
        return kick(invoker, path)
    if a.kick_run:
        return kick_run(invoker, path)
    if a.loop is not None:
        if a.loop < 1:
            print("cockpit-state: --loop wants a whole number of seconds >= 1", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        return loop(invoker, path, a.loop, a.bind_pane)
    return write_once(invoker, path, 5, hw_rev(), a.stdout)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
